# premult

- Label: Premultiply
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/premult.html
- Summary (EN): The Premult node converts an RGBA layer between straight and premultiplied alpha, multiplying or dividing the R, G and B channels by alpha.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Premult convertit un RGBA entre alpha droit et alpha prémultiplié, en multipliant ou divisant RGB par alpha ; la page ne précise pas le cas d'un alpha nul.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to premultiply or un-premultiply", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount, scaled by Mask"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the new result mixes in; default 1 uses only the new value", "Operation: Premultiply by Alpha (multiplies RGB by alpha) or Un-Premultiply by Alpha (divides RGB by alpha)"]

- Caveats: ["The page does not say how zero-alpha pixels are handled during un-premultiply, where division by alpha is undefined; check in practice if layers contain fully transparent pixels."]

